{"etape": 8, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:51:19.532203Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "{\"message\":\"Your balances are:\\n• Gift cards: $327 total ($198 + $129)\\n• Travel certificates: $1,000 total ($500 + $250 + $250)\\n\\nI found your most recent reservation, K1NW8N: round trip from JFK to SFO on May 26, returning May 28, basic economy, for 3 passengers.\\n\\nBecause basic economy flights cannot be changed, I cannot substitute different flights in this reservation. Your available options are:\\n\\nA) Keep all current flights and upgrade them to business: $1,065 per passenger, or $3,195 total. That is $2,628 more than the $567 paid.\\n\\nB) Cancel and rebook the cheapest available business itinerary: HAT023 JFK–SFO on May 26, then HAT204 SFO–SEA and HAT100 SEA–JFK on May 28. The fare is $871 per passenger, or $2,613 total. The reservation was created on May 14 at 4:03 PM EST, so the 24-hour cancellation period ends today at 4:03 PM EST. The cancellation refund would go to the original gift card in 5–7 business days, and the new booking would require separate payment.\\n\\nPlease confirm A or B. If you choose B, also provide the cancellation reason, whether you want travel insurance for the new booking, and which payment method you want to use.\"}"}, "resultat": "Thank you for the balance information.\n\nRegarding my reservation, I'd like to choose option B, to cancel the current reservation and book a new one. My reason for cancellation is that I want to upgrade to business class. I do not need travel insurance for the new booking.\n\nFor payment, I'd like to use my certificates as much as possible, then my gift cards as much as possible, and cover the rest with my Mastercard. I'd like to know how much my Mastercard will be charged. Also, I want to minimize the Mastercard payment, so if cancelling and booking a new one costs less for the Mastercard, I will do it.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:51:37.172344Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "{\"message\":\"I can apply the payments as follows for the Option B itinerary:\\n\\n• New booking total: $2,613\\n• Travel certificate: $500 (only one certificate can be used per reservation, so this is the maximum)\\n• Currently available gift cards: $327\\n• Mastercard charge if rebooked immediately: $1,786\\n\\nThe $567 cancellation refund goes back to the original gift card within 5–7 business days. If you wait for that refund before rebooking, the available gift cards would total $894 and the Mastercard charge would be $1,219, but the fare and seats must be rechecked and are not guaranteed.\\n\\nOption B costs less on the Mastercard than Option A, which would require $2,628 on the Mastercard. Please confirm whether you want to cancel and rebook immediately with a $1,786 Mastercard charge, or cancel now and wait for the refund before rebooking. The 24-hour cancellation period ends today at 4:03 PM EST.\"}"}, "resultat": "I understand that only one certificate can be used per reservation. However, I have three certificates, and I'd like to use all of them.\n\nHere's an idea: can we book three separate reservations? I would use the $500 certificate and all gift cards for myself. Then, I'd like to use certificate_9984806 for Aarav, and the other certificate for Evelyn. I will pay the rest with my Mastercard.\n\nAt the end of the day, I want to know how much my Mastercard will be charged in total across these three separate reservations.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:51:53.643486Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "{\"message\":\"Yes, using three one-passenger reservations would allow all three certificates to be used. The total airfare remains $2,613 (3 × $871).\\n\\nHowever, after applying the $500 certificate to your $871 fare, only $371 in gift-card value can be applied to your reservation; the rest must be used on the other reservations to minimize the Mastercard charge.\\n\\nEstimated total Mastercard charges:\\n• If all three reservations are booked before the $567 refund posts: $1,286 ($1,000 certificates + $327 currently available gift cards).\\n• If you wait for the refund and all $894 in gift cards is available: $719 ($1,000 certificates + $894 gift cards).\\n\\nThe second option has the lowest Mastercard charge, but the fare and seats are not guaranteed to remain available.\\n\\nTo prepare the three bookings, please provide:\\n1. Aarav’s full first and last name and date of birth.\\n2. Evelyn’s full first and last name and date of birth.\\n3. Confirmation that the three passengers will be you, Aarav, and Evelyn, replacing Raj Sanchez and Liam Wilson.\\n4. Confirmation of zero checked bags and no travel insurance for all three reservations.\\n5. Confirmation of whether you want to book immediately or wait for the refund.\\n\\nI will use certificate_9984806 for Aarav and certificate_2765295 for Evelyn unless you specify otherwise.\"}"}, "resultat": "That sounds like a great plan to use all the certificates! I'm happy to proceed with the three separate reservations.\n\nHere's the information you requested:\n\n1.  Aarav's full name is Aarav Sharma, and his date of birth is 07/15/1995.\n2.  Evelyn's full name is Evelyn Chen, and her date of birth is 11/22/1990.\n3.  Yes, the three passengers will be myself, Aarav Sharma, and Evelyn Chen, replacing Raj Sanchez and Liam Wilson.\n4.  Confirmed: zero checked bags and no travel insurance for all three reservations.\n5.  I would like to wait for the refund to minimize the Mastercard charge. I understand that the fare and seats are not guaranteed, but I'm willing to take that chance.\n\nPlease proceed with cancelling the current reservation and preparing for the new bookings once the refund is processed.", "erreur": null}
